    "done_when": "Consolidate the parallel polygon-moment reductions onto one owner. This is the treatment of health review review-code-98773e8b1367 (report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/code-review/98773e8b1367/report.md), which closes the duplicate_owner finding five stored reviews have raised. The candidates are:\n- nova/equilibrium/clip_quadrature.py:155 _straight_edge_monomial_moments;\n- nova/equilibrium/separatrix_clip.py:850 _traced_polygon_moments, with :128 _area_moments and :496 padded_polynomial_current_moments;\n- nova/equilibrium/polygon_moments.py:141 polygon_monomial_moments and :187 polygon_density_moments;\n- nova/equilibrium/stencil_mesh.py:480 fixed_profile_current_moments.\n\nDone when:\n(1) First measure each candidate against exact rational polygon monomial integrals, using sympy or mpmath at 50 digits, on at least 500 polygons. Include sliver triangles below 1e-8 m², near-collinear edges, hex cells and clipped fragments with holes. Print per candidate and per monomial degree the maximum relative and absolute error.\n(2) Choose the owner: the candidate with the smallest maximum error, whichever file holds it. Name it, with its numbers, in the commit and the fragment.\n(3) Delete the other implementations and route every caller to the owner, so a repository search for the deleted names over nova/, tests/, benchmarks/ and scripts/ returns nothing.\n(4) The read-driven current.book rows at 550, 2,000 and 5,000 cells and the clip-moment tests (tests/test_exact_clip_moments.py, tests/test_equilibrium_density_moments.py and the tests covering clip_quadrature.py, separatrix_clip.py, polygon_moments.py and stencil_mesh.py) are unchanged within 1e-13 relative against the base, or improve where step (1) showed the base candidate was the less accurate.\n(5) Negative control: raising inside the owner turns tests/test_exact_clip_moments.py red, by test id.\n(6) Report the net line delta; it must be negative.\n(7) Write an evidence fragment, docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/polygon-moment-owner.html, with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve and the accuracy table; reckon audit-doc must report 0 errors.\n\nDo not edit nova/biot (the moment-path node owns it) or nova/equilibrium/topology.py (the 10,000-cell read node owns it).\n\nRun conditions:\n- Gates run on CPU in place on the fleet allocation, with TMPDIR=/tmp, JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu and the shared interpreter run directly with PYTHONPATH set to the worktree.\n- The current.book certificate rows run as one H200 job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets).\n- Every login-node uv command carries --no-sync, and nothing runs uv sync.\n- Call configure_dtypes() before building any array.\n- Declare any wait as JSON-list wait_probe and wait_terminal on the job that finishes last.\n- Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step, writing the manifest before every wait. Status is complete, blocked or failed.",
